{
 "what": "Flint 40B-A2.5B on a MacBook Pro M5 Pro 48 GB (Mac17,8, macOS 26.5.2), 2026-10-22: one cold request per prompt size and engine, a coding agent's context (bench/corpus.txt, then this repository's source files in path order at 6c13588, cut to the size in Flint's tokens, a random nonce at the start), then a 256-token reply at T 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 20. Points with foreign GPU load were rerun once (the -rerun runs); 'chosen' takes each metric from the run with less foreign load in that metric's window.",
 "prefill_tps": "prompt tokens / time to the first streamed token",
 "decode_tps": "tokens per second between the 16th and the 4th-from-last streamed event",
 "foreign_gpu": "chosen[engine][size]: <metric>_foreign is {run: [mean %, max %, samples]} of non-engine GPU load (gpu_hogs.py, every 2 s) inside that metric's window for every run that measured the point, <metric>_values each run's value, <metric>_run the run with the lower mean (the first sweep on a tie). Built by choose_cells.py from foreign-gpu/ and logs/: rec's windows from its log's request timestamps, Kapitsa's walked back from the sweep's end with its log's durations (about 2 s of error). A decode window (256 tokens, about 2 s) holds 1-2 samples, so the decode choice rests on one or two readings.",
